   Prefer enforcing this later/now with a DB-backed singleton lease if there
   is already a clean, non-schema-changing way to do so.

OR

B. If multiple simultaneous indexer orchestrators are intended to be fully
   supported, STOP and report that an atomic expected-tip precondition around
   RollbackTo is required at the Store boundary.

Do not pretend the current pre-call Tip() read makes the policy atomic.

For this phase I expect policy A is sufficient unless the architecture
already explicitly promises multiple active indexer processes.


